#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054363 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "db1f7851-43e9-5fee-9553-f9d6ead38b40" :question/math-academy-id "e-12675" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P$: Compute the product of the first four prime numbers.\n\n- $Q$: Four is a prime number.\n\n- $R$: Is four a prime number?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false. Rather, it is an instruction.\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $4$ is not a prime number (it is divisible by $2$).\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false. Rather, it is a question, and the possible answers are \"yes\" or \"no.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054364 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f185774-4d55-515c-9032-8f6832c6999a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Truth Value of a Statement"}] :question/id #uuid "8ca6e60c-1411-5f6e-a9f4-d6209f847ddf" :question/math-academy-id "e-12676" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P:$ $4$ is a positive number.\n\n- $Q:$ $2^3$ is a natural number.\n\n- $R:$ $-4 \\geq 2$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate the truth value of each statement:\n\n- Statement $P$ is *true.* Indeed, $4$ is a positive number.\n\n- Statement $Q$ is *true.* Indeed,  $2^3=8$ is a natural number.\n\n- Statement $R$ is *false* because $-4 \\ngeq 2$ .\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054367 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/id #uuid "d85fd26e-50f6-58f1-9e44-8df23863ee6a" :question/math-academy-id "e-12685" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P: \\{5,6,7\\}\\cap \\{6,8,10\\} = \\{6\\}$\n\n- $Q: \\sqrt{3} +2$\n\n- $R: 4\\mid 2$\n\n**Note**: The notation \n\n$$\na\\mid b\n$$\n\nmeans \"$a$ divides $b.$\" This is equivalent to the statement that $b$ is divisible by $a.$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because the intersection of the given sets is indeed the set $\\{6\\}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\n- $R$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $4$ does not divide $2$ (i.e., $2$ is not divisible by $4$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35eba041-5109-5855-b132-174c0271c168" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates"}] :question/id #uuid "a70765b4-08b9-5ebf-92f4-1b7c5266523e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13288" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\n- Subtract $x$ from $10.$\n\n- $y^2 -2  \\leq 3$\n\n- $1+z$ is a perfect square." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it gives an instruction.\n\n- Option II is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $y$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d281e4c-12f3-5079-93f5-be66bce4c00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Compute the sum of the first two natural numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399366} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc90903-d3c5-5540-9c56-a82ad70a2ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set of rational numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399367} {:answer/id #uuid "e4002685-8407-5008-9596-c51979ab7920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The diagonal of a quadrilateral." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399368} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdda3a7-d2ed-58bf-a55c-bd1037a65ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ is a rational number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399369} {:answer/id #uuid "4a90792e-413a-5402-b9c4-94db6437b94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "What is a prime number?" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbdda3a7-d2ed-58bf-a55c-bd1037a65ec2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ is a rational number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399369} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c7d492-3fd1-55b7-9667-7d1d03627d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b625ee5e-9a08-5485-b20f-479dacadfb89" :question/math-academy-id "q-102843" :question/problem "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"$1$ is a rational number.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ea52b5b-53d4-55c2-89b1-9d54b1ec21e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459605} {:answer/id #uuid "15f9454f-19a7-5e3c-990f-fb5fededeb09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15f9454f-19a7-5e3c-990f-fb5fededeb09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459606} :answer-field/id #uuid "75d39554-3208-59d5-ace8-93db5f100923" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460669} {:answer-field/choice