culty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "388254b7-705e-581e-9708-313da2ad5c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-175342" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n- **I.** $P(z):$ Subtract $8$ from $z.$\n- **II.** $Q(x):$ $x÷2$\n- **III.** $R(n):$ $\\sqrt{n}-\\sqrt{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give an instruction.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given statements.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fa39ce5-4b78-55ec-9f01-4f7bd59537c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\pi $ is an irrational number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352417} {:answer/id #uuid "70d9bcf1-e3eb-5236-88ab-e95db6fbda70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The negative numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352558} {:answer/id #uuid "8d307d6b-3d62-5aee-bdbf-9bebf76eb0a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set of the natural numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352798} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7a6ee3-febb-5d40-9985-6bc10b5e3386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The height of a triangle." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352912} {:answer/id #uuid "cca54673-b9a2-585f-a846-9648ba9e245e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Subtract $2$ from $5.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fa39ce5-4b78-55ec-9f01-4f7bd59537c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\pi $ is an irrational number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352417} :answer-field/id #uuid "295d4088-ac28-5602-a22f-48b75fc37e32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87061480-a114-5f8d-a323-725d4db909c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-86473" :question/problem "Which of the following is a mathematical statement?" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. \n\nOf the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"$\\pi $ is an irrational number.\" (This sentence is true.)\n\nAll the other sentences are neither true nor false."}]}
